    "result": "I reported three findings on `ApprovalsController.cs`, all at line 34, the new `_logger.LogInformation` call. I only had the diff, not the full repo, so I couldn't confirm any of them against the code.\n\n1. **Session object logged (security, medium confidence).** `{@Session}` with `CurrentUser` writes the whole user object into the logs. If it carries tokens, session ids, email or claims, anyone who can read the logs can use them to impersonate an Approver. Log only `CurrentUser.Name` or an id.\n2. **Full invoice logged (security, medium confidence).** `{@Invoice}` writes the entire invoice on every approval. That may include bank details, tax ids or addresses, which is a PII and compliance risk. A large or nested invoice can also bloat the logs. Log only the invoice id, status and approver.\n3. **`_logger` may be undefined (correctness, low confidence).** The diff doesn't show a `_logger` field or constructor injection. If `ApiControllerBase` doesn't provide it, the build fails with CS0103.\n\nI found no other defects in the diff.",
